- Cost: $0.0271 vs $0.0351 forecast (77% of forecast) ✅
- Model: z-ai/glm-5.1
- PRD status: completed (true) — succeeded
- Agent role: typescript-engineer — **appropriate** for TypeScript/Next.js/Contentstack SDK work

### AMSD-2041-1 — Live Preview SDK Configuration & useContent Integration
- Elapsed: 3.26 min vs 5.12 min forecast (64% of forecast) ✅
- Cost: $0.3420 vs $0.1601 forecast (213% of forecast) ❌
- Model: moonshotai/kimi-k3 — **cost driver**
- Agent role: typescript-engineer — **appropriate**

### Infrastructure Overhead
- Spec-pass: $0.3118 (no forecast allocated)
- Pipeline (team-lead): $0.0037 (no forecast allocated)

## Recommendations
1. **Model selection**: Use z-ai/glm-5.1 for low-effort implementation tasks. Reserve moonshotai/kimi-k3 for complex multi-file changes requiring deeper reasoning.
2. **Forecast coverage**: Add forecast allocation for spec-pass and pipeline infrastructure steps so total cost variance can be properly assessed.
3. **Cost monitoring**: The 2.1x cost overrun on AMSD-2041-1 suggests the model selection heuristic may be over-provisioning for low-effort tasks.

## Corrective Actions (Agent Role Changes)
No agentRole mismatches detected. The typescript-engineer role is appropriate for all core phase tasks (TypeScript/Next.js/Contentstack SDK configuration and integration work).

No pending stories in future phases require role correction — AMSD-2041 is the only story in the PRD and it is completed.
